First Author: Mete
Title: Predicting Simultaneous Heart Kidney Allocation and Posttransplant Adverse Kidney Outcomes
Source number: 67

Very short summary: This retrospective US national-registry study developed a random forest model using 6,579 adult heart transplant recipients and evaluated it in two temporal external-validation cohorts containing 1,567 and 1,853 recipients. The model predicted a composite of simultaneous heart-kidney transplantation or adverse kidney outcomes within 1 year; in the first external-validation cohort it achieved a c-statistic of 0.899, sensitivity of 68.0%, specificity of 94.1%, PPV of 68.0%, and NPV of 94.1%.

