	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: An expert panel initially selected 44 clinically relevant variables from 531 registry variables. Random-forest Gini importance was then used to select the final 15 predictors. Hyperparameters were exhaustively searched across numbers of trees, maximum depth, maximum features, positive-class weights, and random seeds. Internal five-fold cross-validation was followed by validation in two later temporal cohorts. Interpretability was provided through feature-importance distributions and a patient-level web calculator.

